<description>
Slide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.

Input structure
- The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.
- Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.

Rule
- Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.
- A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.
- A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.
- Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.

Key insight
- Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "black rectangular mask s touching exactly one outer border",
  "path": "straight slide from s to the opposite border along its row band or column band, determined by the touched border",
  "trajectory": "recolor the complete swept row/column stripe orange, then place s at the opposite edge",
  "transform": "all black masks move simultaneously; destination black masks overwrite orange trails and any grey cells, while cells outside swept stripes remain unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-18 rows x 8-14 cols
  colors: black(0), grey(5), orange(7) only
  background: random mix of grey(5) and orange(7); grey fraction 0.2-0.6 of non-black cells
  black_rectangles:
    count: 1-8 solid rectangles
    each_touches: exactly one grid edge (top/bottom/left/right)
    dimensions: 1-6 per side, area 2-18
    depth: perpendicular extent < half the grid dimension on that axis
    no_same_axis_overlap: vertical-moving rects have non-overlapping column bands; horizontal-moving rects have non-overlapping row bands
    multiple_per_edge: allowed (same edge can host multiple rects)
  transformation:
    each rect slides to the opposite edge along its perpendicular axis
    the full column-band (top/bottom rects) or row-band (left/right rects) is recolored orange
    the rect is stamped black at the opposite edge in the same band
    all rects move simultaneously; destination rects overwrite orange trails

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build output, then invert to get input)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dimensions (6-18 rows, 8-14 cols)
    2. Decide number of rects (1-8) and assign each an edge (top/bottom/left/right)
    3. For each rect, pick destination dimensions and position at the OPPOSITE edge, ensuring no same-axis band overlap
    4. Build output grid - fill background with random grey/orange, then paint each stripe orange, then stamp destination rects black
    5. Invert to get input - move each rect from its destination back to its source edge; restore original background in the swept stripe (random grey/orange noise)
    6. Verify each black component touches exactly one edge and is a solid rectangle
