    3. For each rect, pick destination dimensions and position at the OPPOSITE edge, ensuring no same-axis band overlap
    4. Build output grid - fill background with random grey/orange, then paint each stripe orange, then stamp destination rects black
    5. Invert to get input - move each rect from its destination back to its source edge; restore original background in the swept stripe (random grey/orange noise)
    6. Verify each black component touches exactly one edge and is a solid rectangle
